IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pha-offences`
IMPORT `pha-civil`

-- Protection from Harassment Act 2014, Part 3 Division 1 -- worked cases.
--
-- The three asymmetries described in NOTES.md are the point of this file, and
-- most of the assertions exist to pin them down.

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN `the section` IS AN OffenceSection,
      `contravened` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `intended target` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `other person harassed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A TortClaim
DECIDE `a tort claim` `the section` `contravened` `intended target` `other person harassed` IS
    TortClaim WITH
        `the section alleged` IS `the section`
        `the section was contravened in relation to the claimant` IS `contravened`
        `the claimant is the person the respondent intended to harass under section 3` IS `intended target`
        `the claimant is some other person harassed by a section 3 contravention` IS `other person harassed`

`the intended target of a section 3 contravention, suing` MEANS `a tort claim` `section 3` TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a bystander harassed by a section 3 contravention, suing` MEANS `a tort claim` `section 3` TRUE FALSE TRUE
`a section 4 victim, suing` MEANS `a tort claim` `section 4` TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a section 7 victim, suing` MEANS `a tort claim` `section 7` TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a public service worker abused under section 6, suing` MEANS `a tort claim` `section 6` TRUE TRUE FALSE
`someone alleging section 4 where it was not contravened` MEANS `a tort claim` `section 4` FALSE TRUE FALSE

GIVEN `the section` IS AN OffenceSection,
      `contravened` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `convicted` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `caused hurt` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `likely to continue` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `just and equitable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `intended target` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ProtectionOrderFacts
DECIDE `a protection order application` `the section` `contravened` `convicted` `caused hurt` `likely to continue` `just and equitable` `intended target` IS
    ProtectionOrderFacts WITH
        `the section alleged` IS `the section`
        `the respondent has contravened that section in respect of the victim` IS `contravened`
        `the respondent has been convicted of that offence or a Schedule offence in respect of the victim` IS `convicted`
        `the respondent has voluntarily caused hurt to the victim` IS `caused hurt`
        `the respondent is likely to continue or to commit another contravention` IS `likely to continue`
        `it is just and equitable in the circumstances` IS `just and equitable`
        `the applicant is the person the respondent intended to harass under section 3` IS `intended target`

`the intended target of section 3 harassment, applying` MEANS
    `a protection order application` `section 3` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
`a bystander harassed by section 3 harassment, applying` MEANS
    `a protection order application` `section 3` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a section 4 victim, applying` MEANS
    `a protection order application` `section 4` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a public service worker abused under section 6, applying` MEANS
    `a protection order application` `section 6` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- One serious past contravention and no prospect of repetition.
`a single past contravention, nothing likely to follow` MEANS
    `a protection order application` `section 4` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

-- s 12(2A)(b): the respondent assaulted the victim and nothing in ss 3 to 7 is
-- alleged to have been contravened at all.
`a respondent who caused hurt and nothing else` MEANS
    `a protection order application` `section 4` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- s 12(2A)(a): a conviction for a Schedule offence, again with no proved
-- contravention of ss 3 to 7.
`a respondent convicted of a Schedule offence` MEANS
    `a protection order application` `section 4` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE

`everything made out but not just and equitable` MEANS
    `a protection order application` `section 4` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN `the section` IS AN OffenceSection,
      `prima facie contravention` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `imminent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `substantial adverse effect` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `just and equitable expedited` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `intended target` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN ExpeditedFacts
DECIDE `an expedited application` `the section` `prima facie contravention` `imminent` `substantial adverse effect` `just and equitable expedited` `intended target` IS
    ExpeditedFacts WITH
        `the section alleged` IS `the section`
        `prima facie evidence that the respondent has contravened that section` IS `prima facie contravention`
        `prima facie evidence of a conviction for that offence or a Schedule offence in respect of the victim` IS FALSE
        `prima facie evidence that the respondent has voluntarily caused hurt to the victim` IS FALSE
        `the contravention is likely to continue or another is likely imminently` IS `imminent`
        `likely to have a substantial adverse effect on the victim or the victim's day-to-day activities` IS `substantial adverse effect`
        `it is just and equitable for the order to be made on an expedited basis` IS `just and equitable expedited`
        `the applicant is the person the respondent intended to harass under section 3` IS `intended target`

`a stalking victim in imminent danger` MEANS
    `an expedited application` `section 7` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a stalking victim with no substantial adverse effect` MEANS
    `an expedited application` `section 7` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a stalking victim where nothing is imminent` MEANS
    `an expedited application` `section 7` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`a bystander to section 3 harassment seeking an expedited order` MEANS
    `an expedited application` `section 3` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`the intended target of section 3 harassment seeking an expedited order` MEANS
    `an expedited application` `section 3` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE

GIVEN `online` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `written request` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `failed to address` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN EnhancedDamagesFacts
DECIDE `enhanced damages facts` `online` `written request` `failed to address` `reasonable excuse` IS
    EnhancedDamagesFacts WITH
        `the conduct comprises wholly or partly of online activity` IS `online`
        `the victim made a reasonable written request to address the online activity` IS `written request`
        `the respondent failed to address the online activity within a reasonable time` IS `failed to address`
        `the respondent had a reasonable excuse for the failure` IS `reasonable excuse`

`an online campaign, asked to stop, ignored` MEANS `enhanced damages facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
`an online campaign nobody wrote to the respondent about` MEANS `enhanced damages facts` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`an online campaign, asked to stop, taken down promptly` MEANS `enhanced damages facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`an online campaign, asked to stop, with a reasonable excuse` MEANS `enhanced damages facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
`harassment entirely offline` MEANS `enhanced damages facts` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `Section 11 -- which sections found the statutory tort`

#ASSERT `a contravention of this section founds the statutory tort under section 11` `section 3`
#ASSERT `a contravention of this section founds the statutory tort under section 11` `section 4`
#ASSERT `a contravention of this section founds the statutory tort under section 11` `section 5`
#ASSERT `a contravention of this section founds the statutory tort under section 11` `section 7`

-- s 11(1) lists ss 3, 4, 5 and 7. s 6 is not among them.
#ASSERT NOT `a contravention of this section founds the statutory tort under section 11` `section 6`

#ASSERT `a claim lies under section 11` `a section 4 victim, suing`
#ASSERT `a claim lies under section 11` `a section 7 victim, suing`
#ASSERT NOT `a claim lies under section 11` `someone alleging section 4 where it was not contravened`
#ASSERT NOT `a claim lies under section 11` `a public service worker abused under section 6, suing`

§ `Section 12 -- which sections found a protection order`

-- s 12(1) lists ss 3, 4, 5, 6 and 7 -- one more than s 11.
#ASSERT `a contravention of this section founds a protection order under section 12` `section 6`
#ASSERT `a contravention of this section founds a protection order under section 12` `section 4`
#ASSERT NOT `a contravention of this section founds a protection order under section 12` `section 10`

#ASSERT `the court may make a protection order` `a section 4 victim, applying`
#ASSERT `the court may make a protection order` `a public service worker abused under section 6, applying`

-- s 12(2)(b): a past contravention with no prospect of repetition supports no
-- protection order, however serious it was.
#ASSERT `section 12(2)(a) is satisfied` `a single past contravention, nothing likely to follow`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make a protection order` `a single past contravention, nothing likely to follow`

-- s 12(2A): the two deeming routes. Neither needs a contravention of ss 3 to 7
-- to be proved.
#ASSERT NOT `a respondent who caused hurt and nothing else`'s `the respondent has contravened that section in respect of the victim`
#ASSERT `section 12(2)(a) is satisfied` `a respondent who caused hurt and nothing else`
#ASSERT `the court may make a protection order` `a respondent who caused hurt and nothing else`
#ASSERT `section 12(2)(a) is satisfied` `a respondent convicted of a Schedule offence`
#ASSERT `the court may make a protection order` `a respondent convicted of a Schedule offence`

-- The discretion remains.
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make a protection order` `everything made out but not just and equitable`

§ `THE FIRST ASYMMETRY -- the section 3 bystander`

-- s 3(1) makes "the target person or any other person" caused harassment the
-- victim. Illustration 3(c) is a case where the target was harmed without
-- seeing the post; the variant in pha-cases.l4 is one where only a relative was
-- distressed.
--
-- s 11(1) lets "the victim under section 3" sue, and takes s 3's own definition.
-- s 12(9) confines the victim, "for the purposes of this section and section 13",
-- to the person the respondent intended to harass.
--
-- So the bystander has the money remedy and not the forward-looking one. The
-- person with the strongest practical need for an order against the respondent
-- is the one the Act excludes from applying for it.

#ASSERT `a claim lies under section 11` `a bystander harassed by a section 3 contravention, suing`
#ASSERT `a claim lies under section 11` `the intended target of a section 3 contravention, suing`

#ASSERT `the applicant is a victim for the purposes of sections 12 and 13` `the intended target of section 3 harassment, applying`
#ASSERT NOT `the applicant is a victim for the purposes of sections 12 and 13` `a bystander harassed by section 3 harassment, applying`
#ASSERT `the court may make a protection order` `the intended target of section 3 harassment, applying`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make a protection order` `a bystander harassed by section 3 harassment, applying`

-- And the same for the expedited order, because s 12(9) names s 13 too.
#ASSERT `the court may make an expedited protection order` `the intended target of section 3 harassment seeking an expedited order`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make an expedited protection order` `a bystander to section 3 harassment seeking an expedited order`

-- s 12(9) is confined to s 3. A bystander under s 4 -- and s 4's victim is
-- anyone who perceived the conduct and was likely to be harmed -- has both
-- remedies.
#ASSERT `the applicant is a victim for the purposes of sections 12 and 13` `a section 4 victim, applying`
#ASSERT `the court may make a protection order` `a section 4 victim, applying`

-- Stated directly.
#ASSERT `a bystander harassed by a section 3 contravention may sue for damages`
#ASSERT NOT `a bystander harassed by a section 3 contravention may obtain a protection order`

§ `THE SECOND ASYMMETRY -- the section 6 victim`

-- A protection order, yes. The statutory tort, no. The vulnerable-person and
-- intimate-relationship enhancements, no -- s 8A(1) and s 8B(1) list ss 3, 4, 5
-- and 7. And s 14 has abolished the common law tort of harassment.

#ASSERT `a public service worker abused at work may obtain a protection order`
#ASSERT NOT `a public service worker abused at work may sue for damages under this Act`
#ASSERT NOT `a public service worker abused at work may sue in the common law tort of harassment`
#ASSERT NOT `sections 8A and 8B reach this offence` `section 6`

-- Compare the victim of identical conduct who is not a public servant. s 6(1)
-- and s 4(1) use the same five qualities; the difference is only that the s 6
-- victim was at work.
#ASSERT `a claim lies under section 11` `a section 4 victim, suing`
#ASSERT NOT `a claim lies under section 11` `a public service worker abused under section 6, suing`

§ `THE THIRD ASYMMETRY -- what a reasonableness defence answers`

-- ss 3(3), 4(3), 5(3) and 6(4) are each framed as a defence "in any proceedings
-- for an offence". s 7(2) is framed as "subject to subsection (7)". So under
-- s 7 the defence goes to the contravention; under the other four it goes to the
-- offence, and s 11(2) asks about the contravention.
--
-- A READING OF THE WORDS, not a settled proposition -- a court may well read
-- "contravened" in s 11(2) as meaning conduct for which there is no answer. The
-- assertions record the literal reading and the fact that the sections differ.

#ASSERT `the Part 2 defences are expressed as defences to the offence only` `section 3`
#ASSERT `the Part 2 defences are expressed as defences to the offence only` `section 4`
#ASSERT `the Part 2 defences are expressed as defences to the offence only` `section 5`
#ASSERT `the Part 2 defences are expressed as defences to the offence only` `section 6`
#ASSERT NOT `the Part 2 defences are expressed as defences to the offence only` `section 7`

#ASSERT NOT `proving the conduct was reasonable answers the statutory tort` `section 4`
#ASSERT `proving the conduct was reasonable answers the statutory tort` `section 7`

-- Run the same facts through both questions. A s 4 respondent whose conduct was
-- reasonable has contravened s 4(1), so on the literal reading the claim lies;
-- a s 7 respondent whose course of conduct was reasonable has not contravened
-- s 7(1) at all.
`abusive words whose use was reasonable` MEANS Section4Facts WITH
    `the quality of the words, behaviour or communication` IS (Quality WITH `threatening` IS FALSE, `abusive` IS TRUE, `insulting` IS TRUE, `sexual` IS FALSE, `indecent` IS FALSE)
    `used words or behaviour, or made a communication` IS TRUE
    `published identity information of the victim or a related person` IS FALSE
    `heard, seen or otherwise perceived by a person likely to be caused harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation` IS TRUE
    `has a legitimate purpose related to science, medicine, education or art` IS FALSE
    `no reason to believe it would be perceived by the victim` IS FALSE
    `the conduct was reasonable` IS TRUE

`sexual words with a legitimate educational purpose` MEANS Section4Facts WITH
    `the quality of the words, behaviour or communication` IS (Quality WITH `threatening` IS FALSE, `abusive` IS FALSE, `insulting` IS FALSE, `sexual` IS TRUE, `indecent` IS FALSE)
    `used words or behaviour, or made a communication` IS TRUE
    `published identity information of the victim or a related person` IS FALSE
    `heard, seen or otherwise perceived by a person likely to be caused harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation` IS TRUE
    `has a legitimate purpose related to science, medicine, education or art` IS TRUE
    `no reason to believe it would be perceived by the victim` IS FALSE
    `the conduct was reasonable` IS FALSE

-- The s 4(3)(b) defence leaves the contravention standing, so on the literal
-- reading of s 11(2) the claim lies.
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 4(2) is committed` `abusive words whose use was reasonable`
#ASSERT `a section 4 respondent is liable in the statutory tort on the literal reading` `abusive words whose use was reasonable`

-- s 4(1A), by contrast, is a non-contravention and so defeats the claim as well.
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 4(2) is committed` `sexual words with a legitimate educational purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `a section 4 respondent is liable in the statutory tort on the literal reading` `sexual words with a legitimate educational purpose`

§ `Section 11A -- enhanced damages for online activity`

#ASSERT `the court may award enhanced damages under section 11A` `a section 4 victim, suing` `an online campaign, asked to stop, ignored`

-- The written request is a gate. A victim who goes straight to court gets
-- ordinary damages only.
#ASSERT NOT `the court may award enhanced damages under section 11A` `a section 4 victim, suing` `an online campaign nobody wrote to the respondent about`

#ASSERT NOT `the court may award enhanced damages under section 11A` `a section 4 victim, suing` `an online campaign, asked to stop, taken down promptly`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may award enhanced damages under section 11A` `a section 4 victim, suing` `an online campaign, asked to stop, with a reasonable excuse`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may award enhanced damages under section 11A` `a section 4 victim, suing` `harassment entirely offline`

-- And enhanced damages ride on s 11, so the s 6 victim cannot have them either.
#ASSERT NOT `the court may award enhanced damages under section 11A` `a public service worker abused under section 6, suing` `an online campaign, asked to stop, ignored`

-- s 11A(3)(a): no maximum has been prescribed, because no regulations were
-- retrieved.
#ASSERT NOT `a maximum limit on enhanced damages has been prescribed`

§ `Section 13 -- what the expedited order asks for that section 12 does not`

#ASSERT `the court may make an expedited protection order` `a stalking victim in imminent danger`

-- The substantial-adverse-effect requirement has no counterpart in s 12.
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make an expedited protection order` `a stalking victim with no substantial adverse effect`

-- And the future contravention must be imminent, not merely likely.
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make an expedited protection order` `a stalking victim where nothing is imminent`

§ `Section 12(2B) to (2D) -- what an order may contain`

`an exclusion order over premises the respondent owns outright` MEANS OrderContent WITH
    `prohibits the respondent from specified things in relation to the victim` IS TRUE
    `requires the respondent to stop publishing the offending communication` IS FALSE
    `refers a person to counselling or mediation` IS FALSE
    `grants the victim exclusive occupation of the shared residence` IS TRUE
    `the shared residence is solely owned or leased by the respondent` IS TRUE

`an order requiring counselling` MEANS OrderContent WITH
    `prohibits the respondent from specified things in relation to the victim` IS TRUE
    `requires the respondent to stop publishing the offending communication` IS FALSE
    `refers a person to counselling or mediation` IS TRUE
    `grants the victim exclusive occupation of the shared residence` IS FALSE
    `the shared residence is solely owned or leased by the respondent` IS FALSE

`a plain prohibition order` MEANS OrderContent WITH
    `prohibits the respondent from specified things in relation to the victim` IS TRUE
    `requires the respondent to stop publishing the offending communication` IS TRUE
    `refers a person to counselling or mediation` IS FALSE
    `grants the victim exclusive occupation of the shared residence` IS FALSE
    `the shared residence is solely owned or leased by the respondent` IS FALSE

-- s 12(2C): the respondent can be excluded from premises they own outright.
-- s 12(2D): and the order changes nothing about who owns them.
#ASSERT `the order may exclude the respondent from premises the respondent owns` `an exclusion order over premises the respondent owns outright`
#ASSERT `an exclusion order over premises the respondent owns outright`'s `the shared residence is solely owned or leased by the respondent`
#ASSERT NOT `the order affects the respondent's title to the residence` `an exclusion order over premises the respondent owns outright`

-- s 10(1) excepts the s 12(2B)(c) referral, so the therapeutic obligation is the
-- one part of an order that no prosecution can enforce.
#ASSERT `every obligation in this order is backed by the offence in section 10` `a plain prohibition order`
#ASSERT NOT `every obligation in this order is backed by the offence in section 10` `an order requiring counselling`

§ `Section 13B -- the mandatory treatment order`

GIVEN `protection order made` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `expedited only` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `condition likely` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `contributing factor` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `report called for` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A TreatmentFacts
DECIDE `treatment facts` `protection order made` `expedited only` `condition likely` `contributing factor` `report called for` `months` IS
    TreatmentFacts WITH
        `a protection order has been made under section 12(2)` IS `protection order made`
        `only an expedited protection order under section 13 has been made` IS `expedited only`
        `reasonable grounds to believe the respondent is likely to be suffering from a psychiatric condition` IS `condition likely`
        `reasonable grounds to believe that condition is likely to be a contributing factor` IS `contributing factor`
        `a formal assessment report by an appointed psychiatrist has been called for` IS `report called for`
        `the period of treatment required, in months` IS `months`

`a protection order, a psychiatric condition, a report, 24 months` MEANS
    `treatment facts` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 24
`a protection order, a psychiatric condition, a report, 36 months` MEANS
    `treatment facts` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 36
`a protection order, a psychiatric condition, a report, 37 months` MEANS
    `treatment facts` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 37
`only an expedited order, everything else present` MEANS
    `treatment facts` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 24
`a protection order but no assessment report called for` MEANS
    `treatment facts` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 24
`a protection order and a condition that is not a contributing factor` MEANS
    `treatment facts` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE 24

#ASSERT `the court may make a mandatory treatment order` `a protection order, a psychiatric condition, a report, 24 months`
#ASSERT `the court may make a mandatory treatment order` `a protection order, a psychiatric condition, a report, 36 months`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make a mandatory treatment order` `a protection order, a psychiatric condition, a report, 37 months`

-- s 13B(1) is tied to a protection order under s 12(2). The expedited order
-- under s 13 cannot carry one, so the fastest route to protection is the one
-- that cannot reach the cause.
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make a mandatory treatment order` `only an expedited order, everything else present`

-- s 13B(3)(b): the formal assessment report is mandatory, not discretionary.
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make a mandatory treatment order` `a protection order but no assessment report called for`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make a mandatory treatment order` `a protection order and a condition that is not a contributing factor`

§ `Section 14 -- the common law tort is gone`

`a claim in the common law tort of harassment for conduct last year` MEANS HarassmentProceedings WITH
    `brought for the tort of harassment` IS TRUE
    `brought under this Act` IS FALSE
    `the act or conduct occurred before 15 November 2014` IS FALSE

`a claim under section 11` MEANS HarassmentProceedings WITH
    `brought for the tort of harassment` IS TRUE
    `brought under this Act` IS TRUE
    `the act or conduct occurred before 15 November 2014` IS FALSE

`a claim in the common law tort for conduct in 2013` MEANS HarassmentProceedings WITH
    `brought for the tort of harassment` IS TRUE
    `brought under this Act` IS FALSE
    `the act or conduct occurred before 15 November 2014` IS TRUE

`a claim in negligence about the same facts` MEANS HarassmentProceedings WITH
    `brought for the tort of harassment` IS FALSE
    `brought under this Act` IS FALSE
    `the act or conduct occurred before 15 November 2014` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the proceedings may be brought` `a claim in the common law tort of harassment for conduct last year`
#ASSERT `the proceedings may be brought` `a claim under section 11`
#ASSERT `the proceedings may be brought` `a claim in the common law tort for conduct in 2013`

-- s 14(1) abolishes the tort of harassment and nothing else. Another cause of
-- action on the same facts is untouched -- which is all that is left to the s 6
-- victim.
#ASSERT `the proceedings may be brought` `a claim in negligence about the same facts`
